 61CU c  {+61}Cu isotope was produced by bombarding ZrO{-2}                     
 61CU2c  target with 1.4 GeV proton beam at the CERN-ISOLDE facility.           
 61CU3c  Cu isotopes were selectively ionized by the RILIS laser ion source,    
 61CU4c  accelerated to 30 keV, mass separated with the high-resolution mass    
 61CU5c  separator, and injected into the gas-filled linear Paul trap. Measured 
 61CU6c  isotope shift with respect to {+65}Cu using the collinear laser        
 61CU7c  spectroscopy setup. Studied systematics of isotope shifts on {+58-75}Cu
 61CU8c  isotopes. Compared with droplet model predictions.                     
 61CU cL E,J,T$From the Adopted Levels for {+61}Cu in the ENSDF database.       
 61CU c  The systematic uncertainty for isotope shift resulted from             
 61CU2c  uncertainties of the atomic factors M{-k} and F{-k} (2016Bi08).        
